1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,091
Here's a design principle that makes skills work at scale: progressive disclosure.

2
00:00:04,041 --> 00:00:06,008
Think of it like layers of an onion.

3
00:00:06,008 --> 00:00:09,900
The outermost layer is just the name and description — roughly a hundred tokens.

4
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:12,733
That's all the agent sees when deciding whether to trigger.

5
00:00:12,733 --> 00:00:18,141
Once triggered, it reads the full SKILL.md body — the instructions, steps, constraints.

6
00:00:18,141 --> 00:00:22,133
And only when it needs specific reference material does it reach into the references folder.

7
00:00:22,133 --> 00:00:25,658
This keeps context windows lean and the agent focused on what matters right now.

8
00:00:25,658 --> 00:00:28,900
If you're tempted to write a two-thousand-line SKILL.md, stop.

9
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:31,400
Move the bulk into references and link to it.

